<title>USA: Amer BioMed submits 510(k) for catheter.</title>
<headline>Amer BioMed submits 510(k) for catheter.</headline>
<dateline>WOODLANDS, Texas 1997-08-08</dateline>
<text>
<p>American BioMed Inc said Friday that it has submitted to the U.S. Food and Drug Administration a 501(k) for marketing approval of its silicone-based bi-lumen balloon infusion catheters for thrombectomy and thrombolysis.</p>
<p>The company said it expects approval during the fourth quarter of 1997.</p>
<p>According to the company, the 100 percent silicone design of the catheters is resistant to environmental factors, unaffected by body temperature and more bio-compatible than latex balloons or polyvinyl chloride tubing.</p>
</text>
